{
  "_doc": "Shared vectors for matching a typed write-in name to an adult Jotform filing (kindred#2839 follow-up). The server computes each filing's folded name tiers (api/services/jotform_queue.py `name_tiers`); the board's write-in box folds what staff type and matches it against them (frontend/src/components/weekend/filerMatch.ts). Python (tests/unit/api/services/test_jotform_filer_match_parity.py) and Vitest (filerMatch.parity.test.ts) both read this file, so the fold, the Jaro-Winkler score, the tiers and the decisions cannot drift apart. Each match filing carries the tiers the server sends for it, which Python checks against `name_tiers`. Fictional names only.",
  "similar_threshold": 0.85,
  "fold": [
    ["Emma Johnson", "emma johnson"],
    ["  Emma   JOHNSON ", "emma johnson"],
    ["Zoë Chen", "zoe chen"],
    ["José-Luis Garcia", "jose-luis garcia"],
    ["\tOlivia\nChen", "olivia chen"],
    ["", ""]
  ],
